findings.remediation:
Remove the public principal from the bucket policy. Replace
`"Principal": "*"` with specific IAM ARNs, or delete the policy statement entirely if public access was unintentional. Then enable all four
public-access-block settings:
resource "aws_s3_bucket_public_access_block" "this" {
  bucket                  = aws_s3_bucket.this.id
  block_public_acls       = true
  block_public_policy     = true
  ignore_public_acls      = true
  restrict_public_buckets = true
}

Enable deletion protection to prevent accidental destruction:
resource "aws_db_instance" "this" {
  deletion_protection = true
}
For S3, remove `force_destroy = true`. For EC2, set `disable_api_termination = true`.
